  "id": "SPEC-006",
  "purpose": "Give callisto consumers a working, documented mechanism that places CI-built native binary artifacts (napi-rs .node files, maturin wheels) into their platform-stub package directories before `callisto publish` runs, closing the gap between `callisto matrix`'s output and a working end-to-end release, with artifact names that stay unique when multiple packages in one workspace share a target triple.",
  "scope": "Two changes. (1) Rust: `crates/callisto-graph/src/matrix.rs`'s `artifact_name_for_triple(triple: &str) -> String` is replaced with `artifact_name_for_package_platform(package_name: &str, platform: &str, arch: &str, abi: Option<&str>) -> String`, which first sanitizes `package_name` by replacing every `/` character with `-` (because `actions/upload-artifact` forbids `/` in artifact names, and an npm scoped package name such as `@scope/addon` legitimately contains one), then returns `format!(\"{package_name}-{platform}-{arch}\")` when `abi` is `None`, or `format!(\"{package_name}-{platform}-{arch}-{abi}\")` when `abi` is `Some`, using the sanitized `package_name`. This matches napi-rs's own published-platform-package and recommended-CI-artifact-name convention (`<name>-<platform>-<arch>[-<abi>]`, e.g. `@scope/addon-darwin-arm64` on the npm registry becomes artifactName `@scope-addon-darwin-arm64`) rather than the raw Rust target triple. `build_platform_target` (already receiving `package_name` as a parameter) calls `triple_to_role(triple)` to destructure `(platform, arch, abi)` and passes those -- not the raw triple string -- into `artifact_name_for_package_platform`. This embeds the already-workspace-unique `package_name` (a value `PlatformTarget` already carries, sourced from each package's own identity) into `artifactName`, so two different packages declaring the same triple no longer produce colliding CI artifact names. (2) GitHub Actions: extends `.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml`'s existing `callisto-orchestrate` composite-action step -- within the block already guarded by `[[ -n \"$INPUT_PUBLISH\" && \"$INPUT_PUBLISH\" != \"false\" ]]` (action.yml:167), immediately after `NATIVE_MATRIX` is computed, adds a placement loop that downloads each `nativeMatrix` entry's artifact by `artifactName` (pinned to the current run via `$GITHUB_RUN_ID`) and places its contents into `packageDir`. Also updates `.claude/specs/callisto-matrix.md` \u00a76.2, updates `.claude/specs/callisto-matrix.md` \u00a74's artifact-naming-convention section to replace its unsanitized `@scope/addon-darwin-arm64` illustration with the sanitized `@scope-addon-darwin-arm64` and a sentence stating that `packageName` has every `/` replaced with `-` before formatting, and corrects `ARCHITECTURE.md` \u00a712's broken example workflow.",
  "non_goals": [
